engine's program loads, which tells which run configurations start that version.
Values are decimal. "player_*" names are offsets in a player's structure, the others offsets from
game_base unless absolute="true". An empty value means unknown for that version (shown as N/A).
type: int (32 bits, default), float, byte, string or pointer. count: length of an array, pointer
table or string. enum: coded values, as "1:S,2:C". Checked against a running WinMUGEN.
-->
